    "algo": "constrained_grammar_decoding",
    "algoName": "Constrained Grammar Decoding",
    "title": "Rigorous Mathematical Specification and Formal Language Automata of Constrained Grammar Decoding",
    "excerpt": "Constrained Grammar Decoding enforces structured generation (such as valid JSON, SQL, or compiler ASTs) by coupling language model decoding with deterministic finite automata (DFA) or context-free par...",
    "tex": "../decoding/constrained_grammar_decoding/math.tex",
    "pdf": "../decoding/constrained_grammar_decoding/math.pdf",
    "lines": 41,
    "rawTex": "\\documentclass[11pt,a4paper]{article}\n\\usepackage[margin=1in]{geometry}\n\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb,amsthm}\n\\usepackage{algorithm}\n\\usepackage{algpseudocode}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage{hyperref}\n\n\\theoremstyle{definition}\n\\newtheorem{definition}{Definition}[section]\n\\newtheorem{theorem}{Theorem}[section]\n\\newtheorem{lemma}[theorem]{Lemma}\n\\newtheorem{remark}{Remark}[section]\n\n\\title{\\textbf{Rigorous Mathematical Specification and Formal Language Automata of Constrained Grammar Decoding}}\n\\author{Team Scaibu \\\\ \\small Email: \\texttt{jaydeep.9664920749@gmail.com} \\\\ \\small Architecture and Core Engine Team}\n\\date{October 2026}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nConstrained Grammar Decoding enforces structured generation (such as valid JSON, SQL, or compiler ASTs) by coupling language model decoding with deterministic finite automata (DFA) or context-free parsers. At each decoding step, the grammar state identifies the valid allowed token set $\\mathcal{A} \\subset \\mathcal{V}$ and masks invalid logits to $-\\infty$. This specification formalizes logit masking and language containment guarantees.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\section{Mathematical Formulation}\n\nGiven current parse state $q \\in Q$ and vocabulary $\\mathcal{V}$, the transition function defines allowed tokens:\n\\begin{equation}\n\\mathcal{A}(q) = \\{ v \\in \\mathcal{V} \\mid \\delta(q, v) \\ne \\emptyset \\}\n\\end{equation}\nLogit masking:\n\\begin{equation}\n\\tilde{z}_v = \\begin{cases} z_v, & \\text{if } v \\in \\mathcal{A}(q) \\\\ -\\infty, & \\text{if } v \\notin \\mathcal{A}(q) \\end{cases}\n\\end{equation}\n\n\\begin{thebibliography}{9}\n\\bibitem{willard2023} B.~T.~Willard and R.~Louf, ``Efficient guided generation for large language models,'' \\emph{arXiv:2307.09702}, 2023.\n\\end{thebibliography}\n\n\\end{document}\n"
