    "id": "transformer_efficiency__structured_state_space_s4",
    "domain": "transformer_efficiency",
    "domainLabel": "Transformer Efficiency",
    "algo": "structured_state_space_s4",
    "algoName": "Structured State Space S4",
    "title": "Rigorous Mathematical Specification, HiPPO Discretization, and Convolutional Dual of Structured State Space Models (S4)",
    "excerpt": "Structured State Space sequence models (S4) map continuous 1D signals u(t) y(t) through linear ordinary differential equations h'(t) = h(t) + u(t), y(t) = h(t) + u(t) governed by High-order Polynomial...",
    "tex": "../transformer_efficiency/structured_state_space_s4/math.tex",
    "pdf": "../transformer_efficiency/structured_state_space_s4/math.pdf",
    "lines": 38,
    "rawTex": "\\documentclass[11pt,a4paper]{article}\n\\usepackage[margin=1in]{geometry}\n\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb,amsthm}\n\\usepackage{algorithm}\n\\usepackage{algpseudocode}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage{hyperref}\n\n\\theoremstyle{definition}\n\\newtheorem{definition}{Definition}[section]\n\\newtheorem{theorem}{Theorem}[section]\n\\newtheorem{lemma}[theorem]{Lemma}\n\\newtheorem{remark}{Remark}[section]\n\n\\title{\\textbf{Rigorous Mathematical Specification, HiPPO Discretization, and Convolutional Dual of Structured State Space Models (S4)}}\n\\author{Team Scaibu \\\\ \\small Email: \\texttt{jaydeep.9664920749@gmail.com} \\\\ \\small Architecture and Core Engine Team}\n\\date{October 2026}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nStructured State Space sequence models (S4) map continuous 1D signals $u(t) \\mapsto y(t)$ through linear ordinary differential equations $h'(t) = \\mathbf{A}h(t) + \\mathbf{B}u(t), y(t) = \\mathbf{C}h(t) + \\mathbf{D}u(t)$ governed by High-order Polynomial Projection Operators (HiPPO). Discretization via bilinear (Tustin) transforms admits dual computational modes: linear recurrent step updates for $\\mathcal{O}(1)$ inference and non-circular FFT convolutions for parallel $\\mathcal{O}(L \\log L)$ training. This document specifies the discretization operators, stability guarantees, and numerical verification.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\section{Continuous Formulation and Discretization}\n\nGiven step size $\\Delta > 0$, the continuous matrices $(\\mathbf{A}, \\mathbf{B})$ discretize via bilinear transform to:\n\\begin{equation}\n\\bar{\\mathbf{A}} = \\left(\\mathbf{I} - \\frac{\\Delta}{2}\\mathbf{A}\\right)^{-1}\\left(\\mathbf{I} + \\frac{\\Delta}{2}\\mathbf{A}\\right), \\quad \\bar{\\mathbf{B}} = \\left(\\mathbf{I} - \\frac{\\Delta}{2}\\mathbf{A}\\right)^{-1}\\Delta \\mathbf{B}\n\\end{equation}\nDiscrete state updates: $h_k = \\bar{\\mathbf{A}} h_{k-1} + \\bar{\\mathbf{B}} u_k$, with output $y_k = \\mathbf{C} h_k + \\mathbf{D} u_k$.\n\n\\begin{thebibliography}{9}\n\\bibitem{gu2021} A.~Gu, K.~Goel, and C.~R{\\'e}, ``Efficiently modeling long sequences with structured state spaces,'' in \\emph{ICLR}, 2022.\n\\end{thebibliography}\n\n\\end{document}\n"
